From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan <ryan@esterlines.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 02:52:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] LibWeb: Farble hardwareConcurrency and deviceMemory

Off returns the real values. Standard draws hardwareConcurrency in
[2, real] and deviceMemory from the spec buckets capped at the real
bucket, both keyed by the ESO seed. Strict uses 4 cores and the real
memory bucket (8 if the real bucket is 8). Layout tests send an Off
seed so navigator-compatibility-mode-exposure still sees the real
count. The process thread pool is unchanged.
---
